        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>PIA Technical Standard 100 — Standardized Nomenclature for Ram-Air Parachutes</title>\n<script>\nwindow.MathJax = {\n  tex: {\n    inlineMath: [['$', '$']],\n    displayMath: [['$$', '$$']]\n  }\n};\n</script>\n<script defer src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n<style>\n  * {\n    box-sizing: border-box;\n  }\n\n  html,\n  body {\n    margin: 0;\n    min-width: 1650px;\n    min-height: 2118px;\n    background: #fff;\n    color: #080808;\n  }\n\n  body {\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n  }\n\n  .canvas {\n    position: relative;\n    width: 1650px;\n    height: 2118px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    overflow: hidden;\n    background: #fff;\n  }\n\n  .page {\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 122px;\n    left: 199px;\n    width: 1352px;\n    height: 1880px;\n    background: #fff;\n    border: 1.6px solid #111;\n    border-radius: 15px;\n    box-shadow: 17px 17px 17px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.34);\n  }\n\n  .header {\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 164px;\n    left: 88px;\n    width: 1176px;\n    text-align: center;\n  }\n\n  .header-title {\n    margin: 0;\n    font-size: 38px;\n    line-height: 1.08;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n\n  .header-subtitle {\n    margin: 2px 0 0;\n    font-size: 30px;\n    line-height: 1.08;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n\n  .header-date {\n    margin: 2px 0 0;\n    font-size: 25px;\n    line-height: 1.1;\n    font-weight: 400;\n  }\n\n  .rule {\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 330px;\n    left: 88px;\n    width: 1222px;\n    height: 5px;\n    background: #0b0b0b;\n  }\n\n  .document-content {\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 386px;\n    left: 88px;\n    width: 1222px;\n    font-size: 25.5px;\n    line-height: 1.19;\n  }\n\n  h1 {\n    margin: 0 0 36px;\n    font-size: 36px;\n    line-height: 1.12;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n\n  h2 {\n    margin: 0;\n    font-size: 31px;\n    line-height: 1.15;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n\n  .intro-text {\n    margin: 30px 0 0;\n  }\n\n  .address {\n    margin: 30px 0 0;\n    line-height: 1.17;\n  }\n\n  .address strong {\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n\n  a {\n    color: #0000ee;\n    text-decoration: underline;\n  }\n\n  .definitions {\n    margin-top: 66px;\n  }\n\n  .definition-list {\n    margin-top: 29px;\n  }\n\n  .definition-row {\n    position: relative;\n    margin: 0 0 29px;\n    padding-left: 112px;\n  }\n\n  .definition-row .term {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 0;\n    top: 0;\n    width: 105px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n\n  .definition-row .description {\n    margin: 0;\n  }\n\n  .angle-block {\n    position: relative;\n    margin-top: 31px;\n    padding-left: 90px;\n  }\n\n  .angle-heading {\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 0;\n    left: 0;\n    width: 90px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    line-height: 1.15;\n  }\n\n  .sub-definition {\n    margin: 0 0 29px;\n  }\n\n  .sub-definition .subterm {\n    display: inline;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n\n  .area-block {\n    position: relative;\n    margin-top: 30px;\n    padding-left: 90px;\n  }\n\n  .area-heading {\n    position: absolute;\n    top: 0;\n    left: 0;\n    width: 85px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n\n  .area-block .sub-definition {\n    margin-bottom: 28px;\n  }\n\n  .aspect {\n    margin: 28px 0 0;\n  }\n\n  .page-number {\n    position: absolute;\n    bottom: 30px;\n    left: 0;\n    width: 100%;\n    text-align: center;\n    font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n    font-size: 21px;\n    line-height: 1;\n  }\n\n  .change-note {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 200px;\n    top: 2033px;\n    font-size: 25px;\n    line-height: 1;\n    font-style: italic;\n  }\n\n  .appendix-page {\n    position: absolute;\n    right: 99px;\n    top: 2028px;\n    font-size: 28px;\n    line-height: 1;\n  }\n\n  sup {\n    font-size: 65%;\n    vertical-align: super;\n    line-height: 0;\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"canvas\">\n  <main class=\"page\">\n    <header class=\"header\">\n      <p class=\"header-title\">PIA Technical Standard 100</p>\n      <p class=\"header-subtitle\">Parachute Industry Association Publications</p>\n      <p class=\"header-date\">March 27, 2015</p>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"rule\"></div>\n\n    <article class=\"document-content\">\n      <h1>Standardized Nomenclature for Ram-Air Parachutes</h1>\n\n      <section>\n        <h2>Introduction</h2>\n\n        <p class=\"intro-text\">\n          This Technical Standard was adopted by the Parachute Industry Association (PIA) on March 27, 2015.<br>\n          Input concerning revisions and additions should be submitted to:\n        </p>\n\n        <div class=\"address\">\n          <strong>Parachute Industry Association, Inc.</strong><br>\n          Attention:&nbsp; Technical Committee Chair<br>\n          3833 West Oakton Street<br>\n          Skokie, IL 60076<br>\n          Telephone: 847-674-9472<br>\n          Fax: 847-674-9743<br>\n          Email:&nbsp; <a href=\"mailto:TechComChair@pia.com\">TechComChair@pia.com</a>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <section class=\"definitions\">\n        <h2>Definitions</h2>\n\n        <div class=\"definition-list\">\n          <div class=\"definition-row\">\n            <span class=\"term\">Airlock:</span>\n            <p class=\"description\">\n              On a canopy, a valve which permits air flow more easily in one direction, and restricts airflow in\n              the opposite direction.&nbsp; In most case, airlocks are installed in the nose of the canopy to permit air to enter\n              during deployment and flight, and restrict air from flowing out the nose to ensure better pressurization in\n              turbulent air.\n            </p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"angle-block\">\n            <div class=\"angle-heading\">Angle of</div>\n\n            <p class=\"sub-definition\">\n              <span class=\"subterm\">Attack:</span>&nbsp; The angle formed between the flight path and the chord line.&nbsp; The Greek letter alpha (α)\n              is used to denote the angle of attack.&nbsp; See Figure 3.\n            </p>\n\n            <p class=\"sub-definition\">\n              <span class=\"subterm\">Trim:</span>&nbsp; The angle formed between the horizontal reference line and the trim line.&nbsp; The Greek letter\n              theta (θ) is used to denote the angle of trim.&nbsp; Used instead of the somewhat analogous aircraft\n              term “angle of incidence.”&nbsp; See Figure 1b.\n            </p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"area-block\">\n            <div class=\"area-heading\">Area,</div>\n\n            <p class=\"sub-definition\">\n              <span class=\"subterm\">Airfoil Section:</span>&nbsp; The finished cross sectional area of a given rib (airfoil) section.&nbsp; When ribs are\n              not identical, the specific rib must be identified. Used for calculations of pack volume and internal\n              volume of canopy.\n            </p>\n\n            <p class=\"sub-definition\">\n              <span class=\"subterm\">Planform:</span>&nbsp; The product of the average chord times the average span of the canopy.\n            </p>\n\n            <p class=\"sub-definition\">\n              <span class=\"subterm\">Projected:</span>&nbsp; The area of an inflated canopy as viewed from above, perpendicular to the chord line\n              at the centerline of the parachute. Due to canopy curvature and cell inflation bulging the projected\n              area is always smaller than the planform area.\n            </p>\n          </div>\n\n          <p class=\"aspect\">\n            <strong>Aspect Ratio:</strong> Span<sup>2</sup>/Area, which for a rectangular planform reduces to Span/Chord.\n          </p>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n    </article>\n\n    <div class=\"page-number\">Page 1 of 8</div>\n  </main>\n\n  <div class=\"change-note\">Change 1 (December 2015)</div>\n  <div class=\"appendix-page\">A-3</div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
